    "updated_at": "2022-11-30T17:01:29Z",
    "body": "Doing this might help solve a bug. Currently once a browsing context is disowned it seems it can no longer become non-disowned. That seems wrong, especially across origins. But also in a normal case where you set it to null (i.e., disown). Then name target it. And now it's still null except it's not in browsers.\r\n\r\nChatting with @mystor suggests disowned is not really a concept browsers have. Auxiliary is though.",
